Subject: [PATCH] Fix Abseil 20250127 compile-time constexpr failures on some GCC

Abseil 20250127 (bundled with protobuf 6.31 and fetched via FetchContent when no
system Abseil is available, e.g. when cross-compiling or on RHEL8) fails to
compile with several GCC versions because of two unrelated constant-expression
issues. Both are compiler bugs; upstream Abseil keeps the same code, so OpenVINO
patches the fetched source.

1. container/internal/raw_hash_set.h: GetPolicyFunctions() initializes a
   `static constexpr PolicyFunctions value`. Its `get_hash_slot_fn<hasher>()`
   member compares the address of the function template `TypeErasedApplyToSlotFn`
   against nullptr, which those GCCs reject in a core constant expression:
     hash_policy_traits.h:163: error: '(... == 0)' is not a constant expression
   Making `value` `static const` keeps the exact same semantics (a once-
   initialized function-local static) without forcing constant evaluation.

2. strings/ascii.cc: the compile-time self-test
   `static_assert(ValidateAsciiCasefold() == 0, ...)` forces constant evaluation
   of AsciiStrCaseFold, which performs several `static_cast<char>(v)` conversions
   with v > 127. Those implementation-defined conversions are rejected in a
   constant expression by some GCC versions (e.g. RHEL8):
     ascii.cc: error: non-constant condition for static assertion
     ascii.cc: error: overflow in constant expression
   The self-test has no runtime effect (upstream Abseil CI already covers it), so
   remove the ValidateAsciiCasefold() helper and its static_assert.
--- a/absl/container/internal/raw_hash_set.h
+++ b/absl/container/internal/raw_hash_set.h
@@ -4100,5 +4100,5 @@
   static const PolicyFunctions& GetPolicyFunctions() {
-    static constexpr PolicyFunctions value = {
+    static const PolicyFunctions value = {
         sizeof(slot_type),
         // TODO(b/328722020): try to type erase
         // for standard layout and alignof(Hash) <= alignof(CommonFields).
--- a/absl/strings/ascii.cc
+++ b/absl/strings/ascii.cc
@@ -228,27 +228,3 @@
 }
 
-static constexpr size_t ValidateAsciiCasefold() {
-  constexpr size_t num_chars = 1 + CHAR_MAX - CHAR_MIN;
-  size_t incorrect_index = 0;
-  char lowered[num_chars] = {};
-  char uppered[num_chars] = {};
-  for (unsigned int i = 0; i < num_chars; ++i) {
-    uppered[i] = lowered[i] = static_cast<char>(i);
-  }
-  AsciiStrCaseFold<false>(&lowered[0], &lowered[0], num_chars);
-  AsciiStrCaseFold<true>(&uppered[0], &uppered[0], num_chars);
-  for (size_t i = 0; i < num_chars; ++i) {
-    const char ch = static_cast<char>(i),
-               ch_upper = ('a' <= ch && ch <= 'z' ? 'A' + (ch - 'a') : ch),
-               ch_lower = ('A' <= ch && ch <= 'Z' ? 'a' + (ch - 'A') : ch);
-    if (uppered[i] != ch_upper || lowered[i] != ch_lower) {
-      incorrect_index = i > 0 ? i : num_chars;
-      break;
-    }
-  }
-  return incorrect_index;
-}
-
-static_assert(ValidateAsciiCasefold() == 0, "error in case conversion");
-
 }  // namespace ascii_internal
